# Cross-talk matrix T(z_neighbour)/T(z_channel) = (panel height ratio) / (5C control abundance ratio) for 4 channels (6+..9+) x neighbours z=5..11 of ubiquitin [M+zH]z+ (M=8564.8 Da avg).
# Source: bioRxiv v3 p.9 native raster (see SPECTRA_EXTRACTION.md). Heights: panel_h = max pixel-column height inside the window centre+-(3 sigma isotope envelope/z + 2.0 m/z); panel_main = channel main-peak height; control_* = the same in 5C. Uncertainty 'lower'/'upper' = all heights varied by +-1 pixel (0.74 % in 5A, 0.265 % in 5C) -- a 1-px quantisation bound, ~1-sigma-to-2-sigma, NOT a statistical CI.
# kind: measured (>=2x display limit), measured_marginal (1-px bump just above the display limit; real vs chemical noise see p_chance in fig5A_noise_windows.csv), upper-limit (panel shows nothing above the display limit Ldet; UL uses the display limit and the source abundance minus 1 px), unconstrained (source in 5C is itself < 3x its display limit so no bound on T exists; value blank; lower = bound if source were at its maximum allowed).
# Caveats: 5C is a separate 'control' acquisition (direct transfer, no resonant excitation), not the true input to each channel; panels are individually normalised, so only within-panel ratios are used; Orbitrap detector response per charge state cancels in the double ratio.
